<ptxt>
The following controls are also performed when A/C switch is ON.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<emph etype = "bold">
Low speed:
</emph>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Cooling fan operates at low speed when A/C refrigerant pressure is more than specified value of 1.1 MPa (11.2 kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>, 160 psi) or vehicle speed is lower than 30 km/h (19 mile/h).
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<emph etype = "bold">
Middle speed:
</emph>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Cooling fan operates at middle speed for a given time (2 sec.) when fan speed changed to high from low.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<emph etype = "bold">
High speed:
</emph>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Cooling fan speed changes from low to high speed when A/C refrigerant pressure exceeds specified value of 1.8 MPa (18.4 kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>, 261 psi).
</ptxt>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A1611003001">
<title>
Fail-Safe
</title>
<ptxt>
Cooling fan operates at high speed if malfunction related to ECT sensor is detected.
</ptxt>
</servinfosub>
